    "findings": [
      "session-set is emitted by Cookies.set, can emit undefined before generation and can precede completed async initialization.",
      "Session value and local ack cookie do not prove a persisted server session. URL overrides config, then cookie.",
      "Backend PATCH finds same-business public profile ID/session UUID or hash, requires API subscription, returns200 even when attachment is rejected.",
      "Current SessionSerializer.profile is internal contact_id, not the public profile ID used in requests.",
      "Attachment completes asynchronously and fills missing eligible source context, without wholesale conversion or reassignment.",
      "Public identify is queued/received; cached fingerprint can skip a later request. Shopify requires real connected shop/customer ID; arbitrary custom source is unsupported.",
      "forget clears three identity cookies, preserves the session and its existing backend association."
    ]
  },
